Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": ["defensive suppression", "counter strategy", "second-half minus first-half change in opponent scoring (H2-H1)", "halftime adjustment", "team defensive trait", "split-half and cross-season reliability"],
 "methodological_questions": ["Is a team's defensive effect on opponents' H2-H1 change stable across split halves or seasons?", "What number of team-seasons and games is needed to estimate that effect with useful reliability?", "How much of the observed H2-H1 variation is regression to the mean or half-to-half noise?", "Do foul trouble, free-throw mix, leakage, and pace confound H2-H1 comparisons?"],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability (n=102 connectors): Pearson r=+0.215 (p=0.0297), Spearman rho=+0.242, Spearman-Brown about 0.355, sign agreement 65.7%, ICC(player-season)=0.216 with 78.4% of variance within player. Recorded failure evidence: split-half r=0.215 is too low to treat the measure as a stable scoutable trait. Mechanism recorded as A_unanswerable; limited by low measurement reliability."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-018",
   "status_as_recorded": "inconclusive",
   "finding": "Ranked playsheet validation over 10 series: Spearman rho=-0.0639 (p=0.0997, n=665), no clear full-rank signal. Kruskal-Wallis H=32.97 (p=2.7e-05). BEST mean 1.257 (n=56) vs AVOID 1.092 (n=160), U=5546, p=0.004. Trigger accuracy rho=0.4525 (n=121). Limited by leakage, low measurement reliability, and small sample; risks recorded as drift/nonstationarity, leakage, measurement reliability, and sample size."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF15",
   "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
   "finding": "Foul-trouble sequencing after a star's second Q1/Q2 foul: raw lag-1 effect +0.204 (CI +0.163 to +0.245) was produced by free-throw share (41.8% treated vs 9.9% control). Excluding free throws, lag-1 was +0.0486 (CI -0.006 to +0.099, perm p=0.0655), and no lag cleared CI, permutation, and placebo checks. Recorded mechanism: C_artifact; confounding."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-068",
   "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
   "finding": "Possession Control Index incremental R2 over ORtg: headline dR2=+0.139 was driven by leakage correlated with DRtg (corr=+0.894). Offensive-control components added only +0.005 R2 beyond ORtg. Baseline omitted defense by construction. n=120 team-seasons, out-of-sample 2025-26 with 30 teams."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085",
   "what_failed": "Split-half reliability of a derived per-player on-off style measure used as a stable trait",
   "why": "Low reliability (r=0.215, Spearman-Brown 0.355); most variance was within-player half-to-half, so the measure could not be treated as a stable trait."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF15",
   "what_failed": "Lagged opponent PPP after a star's second foul, using all possessions including free throws",
   "why": "Apparent effect was a construction artifact from the free-throw mix; after removing free throws no lag passed the CI, permutation, and placebo tests."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-068",
   "what_failed": "Incremental-R2 claim for a control index over a Net-Rating baseline that omitted defense",
   "why": "Gain came from leakage that tracked the defensive outcome (corr +0.89), so the baseline was mechanically incomplete rather than the index adding information."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-018",
   "what_failed": "Ranked playsheet counter prediction from H1-to-H2 play-type drops",
   "why": "Full-rank Spearman was null (rho=-0.064, p=0.10); only a pairwise BEST vs AVOID difference emerged, with leakage, low reliability, and small samples recorded as limits."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "Within this project's earlier work, split-half reliability of a derived per-entity measure in the NBA data was low (r about 0.2 with n=102), and it was judged insufficient for a stable trait claim (FAM:SF-APPS-085).",
  "Half-to-half and game-level noise in derived NBA halves/splits has produced artifacts and null results when the measure was built from play-by-play without strict controls (FAM:SF15, FAM:SF-APPS-068, FAM:SF-APPS-018).",
  "Free-throw mix and leakage are documented confounders in this project's possession-level analyses (FAM:SF15, FAM:SF-APPS-068)."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "No retrieved record tests whether a team's defensive effect on opponents' H2-H1 change is reliable. FAM:SF-APPS-085 concerns connector players, not team defense or H2-H1 change.",
  "No retrieved record reports a team-level split-half or cross-season reliability for any defensive measure.",
  "No retrieved record gives the sample size needed for a team-level H2-H1 reliability estimate with 120 team-seasons.",
  "The records do not show whether the 2022-23 to 2025-26 seasons have stable rules or coaching patterns that would make cross-season comparison valid."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "H2-H1 is a difference of two noisy half-game measures. Its reliability will be lower than either half's reliability, so a team trait claim is harder to support than for the halves alone.",
  "120 team-seasons means about 30 teams over 4 seasons, with repeated teams, so teams are not independent units and cross-season effective sample size is smaller than 120.",
  "Team-level H2-H1 effects are likely dominated by game-level and situational noise (foul trouble, free-throw share, garbage time, pace, opponent quality) unless these are explicitly controlled.",
  "The question as posed asks for reliability, but the naive test (correlate team H2-H1 effects across seasons) would also pick up stable team quality and style, not only the defensive-trait claim."
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "The full text of the retrieved records was not read (read_family not called), so exact n, controls, and thresholds beyond the summaries are unknown.",
  "FAM:SF-APPS-086 was referenced as related by FAM:SF-APPS-085 but was not returned by retrieval and is not cited.",
  "Data-level details such as how H1/H2 are defined in overtime and how partial possessions enter the team-level effect are not in the task statement.",
  "Whether 2025-26 playoff data (complete as of 2026-06-21) is comparable to regular-season data is unknown."
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes",
  "explanation": "Without the retrieved records the question could have been pre-registered as a plain cross-season correlation test. The prior low-reliability result (FAM:SF-APPS-085) and the foul and leakage artifacts (FAM:SF15, FAM:SF-APPS-068) show that a derived split-based measure from this data is likely to be noisy and artifact-prone. That supports a reliability-first gate before any claim that the trait is real, rather than proceeding directly to the effect test."
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": 0.3,
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
    "text": "The H2-H1 effect is a difference of two noisy halves; reliability of the team-level estimate is not shown to be adequate, and FAM:SF-APPS-085 found low reliability for a similar derived measure."
   },
   {
    "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
    "text": "120 team-seasons (about 30 teams x 4 seasons) is a small, non-independent sample for detecting a stable team trait in a noisy difference score."
   },
   {
    "code": "CONFOUNDING",
    "text": "Foul trouble, free-throw share, pace, opponent strength, and garbage time can drive H2-H1 differences (FAM:SF15)."
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "no",
  "cited": ["FAM:SF-APPS-085", "FAM:SF15", "FAM:SF-APPS-068", "FAM:SF-APPS-018"],
  "summary": "No retrieved record answers whether team defensive effects on opponents' H2-H1 change are reliable. The closest record (FAM:SF-APPS-085) shows low split-half reliability for a different per-player measure with n=102. Other records show artifacts and nulls from related play-by-play constructions, supporting caution about confounding and leakage."
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
   "text": "Difference-score reliability of H2-H1 is likely low; FAM:SF-APPS-085 found low reliability for a comparable derived measure."
  },
  {
   "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
   "text": "120 team-seasons with repeated teams gives limited effective sample size for a trait claim."
  },
  {
   "code": "CONFOUNDING",
   "text": "Free-throw mix, foul trouble, pace, opponent quality, and garbage time can produce H2-H1 differences unrelated to defense (FAM:SF15)."
  },
  {
   "code": "LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD",
   "text": "Any defensive measure built from the same game's second half can leak outcome information into the H2-H1 estimate (FAM:SF-APPS-068, FAM:SF-APPS-018)."
  },
  {
   "code": "MECHANICAL_FLOOR",
   "text": "Team defense and opponent scoring are mechanically linked to net rating, so a defensive H2-H1 effect can partly reflect shared scoring structure (FAM:SF-APPS-068)."
  },
  {
   "code": "RTM_SELECTION",
   "text": "Selecting teams with extreme H2-H1 defensive effects in one season and testing them in another will overstate persistence."
  },
  {
   "code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY",
   "text": "Rule, pace, and coaching changes across 2022-23 to 2025-26 can shift H2-H1 patterns, weakening cross-season reliability (FAM:SF-APPS-018)."
  },
  {
   "code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING",
   "text": "Multiple split definitions, play types, and H2-H1 variants increase the chance of a spurious reliable-trait result."
  },
  {
   "code": "BASE_RATE",
   "text": "Low base rates of true team-level H2-H1 differences would make a positive reliability claim hard to support at this sample size."
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": 0.05,
  "rejected": 0.2,
  "untestable": 0.25,
  "artifact": 0.1,
  "uncertain": 0.4
 },
 "decision": "do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "Minimum viable test: reliability of team-level defensive effect on opponents' H2-H1 PPP change, estimated as split-half (odd/even games within season) and cross-season intraclass correlation, with a Spearman-Brown correction. Only if reliability is adequate should a trait claim follow.",
  "unit": "Team-season (30 teams x 4 seasons, about 120 units), with games nested within team-season; also game-level for split-half estimates.",
  "sample": "NBA 2022-23 to 2024-25 regular seasons (complete) plus 2025-26 regular season only from 2026-04-13 onward; playoffs excluded from the reliability test or analysed separately. Freeze the data version before analysis; 2025-26 playoffs are complete as of 2026-06-21 but should not be pooled without a comparability check.",
  "power": "Before analysis, simulate the sampling distribution of split-half and cross-season ICC at 120 team-seasons. Proceed to a trait claim only if the lower 95% bound of reliability exceeds a pre-set threshold (for example 0.5); otherwise report as untestable at this sample size.",
  "controls": "Adjust H2-H1 for free-throw share, foul counts, pace, opponent strength, and garbage-time filtering (margin threshold). Exclude possessions after the first 'garbage' margin. Use defensive matchup minutes for opponent-adjusted estimates. Avoid any leakage: define the defensive measure from data available before the H2 window it is compared against.",
  "falsification": "Pre-register that a reliability ICC below threshold, or a null correlation between split-half estimates, falsifies the trait claim. Include a placebo H1-H1 split (first half versus an earlier split) to check whether the reliability is specific to H2-H1 or reflects generic team quality.",
  "multiplicity": "Pre-register one primary reliability estimate (odd/even games within season, cross-season ICC). Treat other play types and H2-H1 variants as exploratory with Holm correction.",
  "decision_rule": "Support a trait claim only if the primary split-half and cross-season reliabilities both exceed the pre-set threshold, the H1-H1 placebo does not show the same reliability, and the effect survives the free-throw, foul, pace, and garbage-time adjustments. Otherwise report as uncertain or untestable.",
  "data_version": "Frozen NBA stats API play-by-play, substitution, starters, and matchup-minute files as of 2026-10-06; 2025-26 regular season used only after 2026-04-13 completion; 2025-26 playoffs excluded from the primary analysis, with the versioned extract recorded."
 }
}

